        "test_procedure": "1. Locate the cell_to_coset_evals function (SG-001) in the codebase.\n2. Verify the function signature and return type: it MUST return a CosetEvals with exactly FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_CELL elements.\n3. CRITICAL: Trace the input cell bytes from P2P message deserialization to this function.\n4. Identify the byte slicing logic: each segment [i*BYTES_PER_FIELD_ELEMENT : (i+1)*BYTES_PER_FIELD_ELEMENT] must extract exactly BYTES_PER_FIELD_ELEMENT bytes.\n5. Test undersized cell input: craft a P2P message with a cell shorter than expected (less than FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_CELL * BYTES_PER_FIELD_ELEMENT bytes).\n6. Verify behavior with undersized cells: (a) check if the function detects the short input, (b) confirm it rejects with appropriate error rather than producing undersized field elements.\n7. Test edge cases: (a) cell exactly one byte short, (b) cell missing one complete field element, (c) empty cell, (d) cell with extra trailing bytes.\n8. Check the Cell byte length check validation layer: verify it executes BEFORE cell_to_coset_evals is called.\n9. Test: bypass or disable the length check and verify cell_to_coset_evals has secondary defense.\n10. Verify CosetEvals output invariant: confirm the returned array always has exactly FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_CELL elements, no more, no fewer.\n11. Check for panic/crash conditions: if byte slicing encounters insufficient data, does it panic or return error?\n12. Verify field element deserialization: each BYTES_PER_FIELD_ELEMENT byte segment must be valid field element bytes.\n13. Test: inject invalid field element bytes (e.g., value >= field modulus) and verify proper rejection.\n14. Cross-reference with cell verification logic: ensure cells pass integrity checks before reaching this function.\n15. Verify memory safety: in memory-unsafe languages, confirm no buffer over-read when cell is undersized.",
        "bug_class": "Input Validation / Data Integrity",
