        "test_procedure": "1. Locate both functions: cell_to_coset_evals (SG-001) and coset_evals_to_cell (SG-002) in the codebase.\n2. Understand the transformation: cell_to_coset_evals converts a Cell (byte array) into CosetEvals (array of field elements), and coset_evals_to_cell reverses this.\n3. CRITICAL: Design a falsification test - attempt to find a valid cell input where the roundtrip produces a different result.\n4. Test with canonical cell values: create cells with various valid field element byte representations and verify roundtrip equality.\n5. Test boundary field elements: (a) zero element (all zero bytes), (b) one element, (c) maximum valid field element (modulus - 1), (d) elements near modulus boundary.\n6. Test structured patterns: (a) alternating bytes, (b) repeated patterns, (c) cells derived from actual blob data.\n7. Verify byte-level equality: the comparison must be exact byte equality, not just field element equality.\n8. Check for serialization/deserialization asymmetry: ensure the byte representation used by coset_evals_to_cell matches what cell_to_coset_evals expects.\n9. Check for normalization issues: if field elements can have multiple byte representations, verify consistent normalization.\n10. Trace through the codebase: identify where this roundtrip is relied upon in the cell recovery/reconstruction flow.\n11. Test with recovered cells: after recover_cells_and_kzg_proofs, verify that reconstructed cells pass the roundtrip test.\n12. Check endianness: verify both functions use consistent byte ordering (big-endian vs little-endian).\n13. Verify FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_CELL alignment: ensure both functions process exactly the same number of elements.\n14. Property-based testing: if available, use fuzzing to generate random valid cells and verify roundtrip holds.\n15. Impact analysis: if violated, recovered cells would differ from original cells even with a correct polynomial, causing invalid sidecars and potential consensus failures.",
        "bug_class": "Data Integrity / Serialization Error",
        "risk_category": "Tampering",
        "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B14-28, Invariant: SG-002:INV-002, Primary Element: SG-002:coset_evals_to_cell, Covered Nodes: actor-validator-node. This is a fundamental correctness property for cell serialization. Violation would cause recovered cells to differ from originals, producing invalid blob sidecars. While classified as internal-only, the impact propagates to consensus if sidecars fail verification. The test should attempt to FALSIFY the invariant by finding edge cases where roundtrip fails.",
